  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_009: pca_n2000, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) achieved 58.6% accuracy at 4.55 GPU hours. The biggest uncertainty is whether the simple linear PCA encoder is a bottleneck for the RNA modality. Config_017 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 (a learned VAE) while keeping all other settings identical (multimodal, multiprofile, ViT-L, transformer, weighted), giving a clean single-variable ablation. If scvi improves accuracy, it confirms that non-linear RNA representations matter and motivates trying scgpt next; if it does not, PCA is sufficient and we can redirect effort toward fusion or aggregation. This is the highest-information experiment for resolving the RNA-encoding question. Expected cost is moderate, roughly 5–6 GPU hours (slightly above config_009's 4.55) due to the VAE training overhead, which is acceptable given 8 experiments remain."
}

